# API Domains

Expose distinct resources as **separate serverless microservices**. Domains required: **stock**, **transactions**, **customers**, **deliveries**.

## Suggested contracts

| Domain | Service | Examples | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Stock / products | `services/products` | `GET /products/:id`, `GET /products/:id/stock` | Read-only catalog; seed only |
| Customers | `services/customers` | `POST /customers`, `GET /customers/:id` | Buyer identity |
| Deliveries | `services/deliveries` | `POST /deliveries`, `GET /deliveries/:id` | Address / recipient |
| Transactions | `services/transactions` | `POST /transactions` → `PENDING`; `GET /transactions/:id` | Ledger + provider charge |

## HTTP & validation

- Use `201` create, `200` read/update, `400` validation, `404` missing, `409` stock conflict, `502` provider failure.
- Validate every input for real scenarios (missing fields, invalid card shape, insufficient stock, duplicate payment, invalid email/phone/address); apply shared OWASP headers + logger on every route.
- Use **distinct request types** per domain (mix of GET/POST/PATCH as needed) — required by brief for stock, transactions, customers, deliveries.
- Business rules live in use-cases, **never** in controllers/handlers.
- Document all endpoints in OpenAPI under `docs/api/` (Apidog-importable) and keep Nest Swagger decorators in sync — see `apidog-openapi` rule. Update docs on every route create/change.
- Amounts: product price + always-on base fee + delivery fee; persist fee breakdown on the transaction.
